cative\nenergy, E(A, A).\n1. Introduction\nThe sumset of a ﬁnite set of an additive group, A, is deﬁned by\nA + A = {a + b : a, b ∈A}.\nThe productset and ratioset are deﬁned in a similar way.\nAA = {ab : a, b ∈A},\nand\nA/A = {a/b : a, b ∈A}.\nA famous conjecture of Erd˝os and Szemer´edi [4] asserts that for any\nﬁnite set of integers, M,\nmax{|M + M|, |MM|} ≥|M|2−ε,\nwhere ε →0 when |M| →∞. They proved that\narXiv:0806.1040v2  [math.CO]  18 Jun 2008\nmax{|M + M|, |MM|} ≥|M|1+δ,\nfor some δ > 0. In a series of papers, lower bounds on δ were ﬁnd.\nδ ≥1/31 [7], δ ≥1/15 [5], δ ≥1/4 [2], and δ ≥3/14 [10]. The last two\nbonds were proved for ﬁnite sets of real numbers.\nDate: July 22, 2008.\nResearch was supported by OTKA and NSERC grants and by a Sloan Fellowship.\nsolymosi@math.ubc.ca.\n1--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Sum–Product Conjecture (https://blog.georgeshakan.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/talk5.pdf)\nciteturn7search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.0 years ago; József Solymosi ... # Bounding multiplicative energy by the sumset ☆ ... The <i>sumset</i> of a finite set of an additive group, A, is defined by\nJózsef Solymosi\n\nAvailable online at www.sciencedirect.com  \nScienceDirect  \nAdvances in Mathematics 222 (2009) 402–408  \nELSEVIER  \nADVANCES IN Mathematics  \nwww.elsevier.com/locate/aim\n\n# Bounding multiplicative energy by the sumset ☆\n\nJózsef Solymosi\n\nUniversity of British Columbia, Mathematics, 1984 Mathematics Road, Vancouver, British Columbia, V6T 1Z2, Canada  \nReceived 23 June 2008; accepted 15 April 2009  \nAvailable online 25 April 2009  \nCommunicated by Gil Kalai\n\n<table id=\"e1\">\n<tr><td><b>Abstract</b></td></tr>\n<tr><td>We prove that the sumset or the productset of any finite set of real numbers, A, is at least |A|<sup>4/3−ε</sup>, improving earlier bounds. Our main tool is a new upper bound on the multiplicative energy, E(A, A).</td></tr>\n<tr><td>© 2009 Elsevier Inc. All